<title>UK: Shire says makes &quot;excellent&quot; progress.</title>
<headline>Shire says makes &quot;excellent&quot; progress.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain's Shire Pharmaceuticals said on Tuesday it had made good progress in a few key commercial and research programmes which was likely to boost its future performance.</p>
<p>Among its various programmes, Shire said its trials on Chronic Fatigue Syndrome Galantamine would enter the second stage this month.  </p>
<p>The company also said it expected its product to treat kidney disease, Lambda, to progress into Phase II studies starting in June.</p>
<p>Shire's shares firmed 2.0p to 219 by 0830 GMT. --London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
